  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Checkpoint Questions\n\n1. **What's the difference between SOURCE_CONFIG and DESTINATION_CONFIG?**\n   - Answer: SOURCE_CONFIG is where data comes from, DESTINATION_CONFIG is where it goes\n\n2. **How do you make a bidirectional bridge?**\n   - Answer: Add multiple mappings with different DIRECTION values (\"in\" and \"out\")\n\n3. **What port does Mosquitto use externally in our setup?**\n   - Answer: Port 1884 (maps to internal port 1883)\n\n---"
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Summary\n\n### Key Concepts Learned\n- MQTT bridges connect different brokers\n- SOURCE_CONFIG and DESTINATION_CONFIG define endpoints\n- MAPPING defines topic transformation and direction\n- Direction options: \"out\", \"in\", or \"both\"\n- Actions can process bridged data\n\n### Available Brokers for Testing\n| Broker | Use Case |\n|--------|----------|\n| `mosquitto_bridge` (port 1884) | Local bridge testing |\n| `iot.coreflux.cloud` (port 1883) | Cloud demonstrations |\n\n---\n\n**Next Tutorial:** [Database Routes](./database-routes.lotnb) - Learn data persistence with PostgreSQL"
  }
]